<!--
    kuna-switchguardmerge-default: the switch's default is the outlier test
    (option switchguardmerge).

    Source (x86-64, clang -O2):
      unsigned uns(unsigned x) {
        switch (x) {
        case 10: return f0(x); ... case 16: return f6(x);
        case 1000: return f8(x + 1);
        default: return 7;
        }
      }

    clang sends every value outside 10..16 to a block testing x == 1000, which
    the guard folding makes the switch's default.

    Stage: P2/switchnorm, ActionSwitchGuardMerge: an equality chain that is
    the switch's default (entered from the switch alone) becomes cases, and
    its last miss the default.

    Pass 1 (default) prints case 1000 and default: return 7; pass 2
    (switchguardmerge off) the test after the switch.
-->
